[size=4][b]PalSchema Hub — Community Schema Registry[/b][/size]

[b]On Palworld 1.0.3? Your mods are fine.[/b]
The whole 1.0.2 patch line (v1.0.2, v1.0.2.100993 "Mod Support Improvement", v1.0.2.101103) and 1.0.3 ("Balance Adjustments & Bug Fixes") changed [b]no[/b] DataTable row structs — every field that existed in 1.0 still exists, unchanged. That is verified, not assumed: the decompiled SDK has not been regenerated since 1.0 (head 62fad41, 11 Jul 2026). Check any mod yourself in one line:
[code]npx palschema-validate --migrate 1.0.2..1.0.3 my-mod/
-> no row-struct changes between 1.0.2 and 1.0.3 (both alias Palworld 1.0, SDK 62fad41)[/code]
[b]New in 1.5 — 1.0.3 item values, and int columns are enforced.[/b]
1.0.3 was a balance patch: it changed no row structs, but it did change row [i]values[/i]. The item reference was re-scraped, so World Tree Holy Water now weighs 0.1 instead of 1 and the Aquatic Construction Kit is rank 2 instead of 4. If you copy item rows as a base for your own, you were copying two stale numbers.
Separately, 158 fields the game declares as whole numbers (DT_PalDropItem.Level, DT_PalHumanParameter.MeleeAttack and others) used to accept a fractional value like 1.5 and only misbehave in-game. They now fail validation where you can see them:
[code]DT_PalDropItem > Alpaca /Level: must be integer[/code]
Also verified compatible with PalSchema 0.6.3, checked against its full 0.6.0-to-0.6.3 diff rather than the release notes: no field renamed, no path moved, no row validation changed.

[b]Previously, in 1.4 — unknown fields warn instead of failing your build.[/b]
If your mod sets a field this registry does not know about, the validator now prints a warning with a did-you-mean suggestion and still exits 0:
[code]WARN mods/pals.json:Lamball unknown field "rarity" — did you mean "Rarity"?
1 file validated, 0 errors, 1 unknown-key warning[/code]
These schemas are derived from a snapshot of the game's SDK headers, so every field Palworld adds [i]after[/i] that snapshot used to be a hard rejection of perfectly correct mod JSON. Now a stale schema degrades to a warning you can ignore, never a blocked build — while wrong types and malformed rows still fail. Add [b]--strict[/b] to turn those warnings back into errors for CI. PalSchema's own pseudo-keys ($Filters, and the {"Action": "Clear", "Items": [...]} wrapper accepted on array fields) never warn. These are the semantics PalSchema itself is adopting (its issue #134).

[b]What is this?[/b]
A free, browsable database of every field you can touch in PalSchema raw-table mods — the answer to "where are all the game variable names?" ([url=https://github.com/Okaetsu/PalSchema/issues/53]PalSchema issue #53[/url]).

[list]
[*][b]Browse the schemas:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/]booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub[/url] — 31 gameplay DataTables (DT_PalMonsterParameter, DT_ItemDataTable, DT_ItemRecipeDataTable, DT_BuildObjectDataTable, DT_PalDropItem, DT_WazaDataTable, ...), searchable, with every field name, type, example values and enum value lists.[/*]
[*][b]Item value reference:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/items.html]items.html[/url] — [b]2,445 current-game items (Palworld 1.0.3)[/b] with their ItemActorClass / ItemStaticClass / ItemDynamicClass, SortId, Rarity, Defense / Health / Durability and full row JSON to copy. Rarity variants are separate rows, as the game stores them (PlasticHelmet, PlasticHelmet_2 .. _5). (Cloning an armour row without ItemActorClass is why a custom helmet shows bare hair in-game.)[/*]
[*][b]Version diff:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/diff.html]diff.html[/url] — what changed in the game's row structs between any two Palworld versions, now including 1.0.3.[/*]
[*][b]GitHub repo:[/b] [url=https://github.com/Booyaka101/palschema-hub]github.com/Booyaka101/palschema-hub[/url] (MIT)[/*]
[*][b]Validator CLI:[/b] checks your mod JSON against the registry and reports typed field errors (typo'd or renamed fields, wrong types) [i]before[/i] you launch the game:
[code]npx palschema-validate --version 1.0 my-mod/DT_PalMonsterParameter.json[/code]
[/*]
[/list]
[b]Did a game patch break your mod?[/b]
A Palworld update can add, remove or rename DataTable fields — and a mod setting a field the game no longer has just silently does nothing. This scans your mod against the real field-level delta between two versions:
[code]npx palschema-validate --migrate 0.7.2..1.0 my-mod/[/code]
It prints one line per affected field and exits 1 if anything broke, so it works in CI:
[code]my-mod.json > DT_PalMonsterParameter > ChickenPal000 > OverridePartnerSkillTextID: removed in 1.0 (was FName) — possible rename to OverridePartnerSkillNameTextID (medium confidence)[/code]
For the big one: across the 30 covered registry tables, Palworld 1.0 removed exactly [b]one[/b] field — OverridePartnerSkillTextID on PalCharacterParameterDatabaseRow (hitting both DT_PalMonsterParameter and DT_PalHumanParameter), replaced by the split pair OverridePartnerSkillNameTextID + OverridePartnerSkillDescTextID. It also added 23 fields you can now use, including EnemyWazaCoolTimeRate and BestWorkSuitability. Rename suggestions are a labelled heuristic, never a silent guess. 0.7.3, 1.0.1, the 1.0.2 line and 1.0.3 changed no row structs at all, and the tool says so rather than inventing a diff.

[b]How current is each part? (please read before trusting a value)[/b]
Field [b]names and types[/b] — the schemas, the version diffs, the --migrate scan — are verified against the [b]current[/b] game's row structs (PalworldModdingKit SDK headers @62fad41). That part is 1.0.3-current, and it includes post-1.0 additions (InstallMaxNumInBaseCamp, CraftExpRate, drop item slots 6–10), renames (RedialIndex→SortId, HP→Hp), both array patch forms ([...] replaces, {"Action": "Clear", "Items": [...]} clears/appends) and $Filters wildcard metadata. Proven against real published PalSchema mods.
Row [b]values[/b] in the item reference are [b]current too, re-scraped for 1.0.3[/b]. They come from paldb.cc, which tracks the live build (its footer pins to v1.0.3, 12 Aug 2026): [b]2,445 rows[/b], up from the 947 rows of Jan-2024 dump data this page used to ship. Items added since 1.0 are finally present — Hexolite Helmet (internal Code SFHelmet, SortId 1325) among them — and the dead field [b]SortID[/b], which the current game renamed to SortId, is gone. Fields paldb.cc does not render (VisualBlueprintClassSoft, DropItemType, GrantEffect*, TechnologyTreeLock and friends) are filled from the old Jan-2024 dump where that row existed back then; paldb wins every conflict, and items.json records per row exactly which fields are live and which are legacy fill. A gate in CI validates every row against the DT_ItemDataTable schema and fails the build if the data ever goes stale again.

[b]What the download contains:[/b] a complete offline copy of the registry — all 31 JSON Schemas, the machine-readable index, the searchable browser page, the item value reference, the version-diff viewer with all 12 version snapshots and every pairwise diff, and the validator CLI (MIT). Look up any field in a text editor with no tools at all, or validate and migration-scan your mod fully offline (the migration scan needs no npm install at all). The links above always carry the latest version. No game assets are included.

Credits: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/palworld/mods/2361]PalSchema[/url] by Okaetsu. Data derived via public community dumps (blaynem/paldex) and the PalworldModdingKit SDK headers (localcc).